  "notes": "The chord-forward end of the Drake orbit, and the one place on this bench where sevenths outnumber triads: `extensions` runs 0.30/0.45/0.25 with dorian weighted level with natural minor, which is what \"minor and dorian with 7th/9th extensions and modal borrowing\" means in parameters. The rhythmic signature the research names is a kick with a strong and-of-2 push, so `secondaryAnchor` is `2&` — the only entry in this batch that moves it off beat 3 — with `offbeat8thShare` 0.3 beside it. Roomy claps become a wide `layerClapOffsetMs` of 4–10 ms and filtered percussion a shaker/rim/perc set on the offbeat. The 808 glides slowly between chord roots (`glideProb` 0.7, `portamentoMs` up to 280) because the low end here is blended with a filtered sample bass rather than punched. A real counter-line sits over the bed at `densityRatio` 0.5. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium; the extension weights in particular are my reading of \"7th/9th extensions\", which is named without figures.",
